#chip 16F877A, 20

'Change1657 test: #option StringLimitCheck clamps an over-long literal assignment to the
'destination's declared length instead of overrunning adjacent RAM (14-bit PIC/SysReadString).
'Expect: compiles; the W register is loaded with BUF_STRING_LENGTH (5) immediately before
'the call to SYSREADSTRING (confirmed by comparing the generated .asm with and without this
'option: without it, no such movlw/BUF_STRING_LENGTH line precedes the call at all).

#option StringLimitCheck
#option explicit

Dim Buf As String * 5
Buf = "ABCDEFGHIJ"   'Longer than Buf's 5-character buffer: clamped to "ABCDE", not overrun

Do
Loop
